<title>NORWAY: Statoil's Heidrun oilfield begins 11-day shutdown.</title>
<headline>Statoil's Heidrun oilfield begins 11-day shutdown.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>State oil company Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Monday it had begun a scheduled 11-day maintenance shutdown at the Heidrun oilfield in the Norwegian Sea.</p>
<p>&quot;The Heidrun field began an annual maintenance shutdown today,&quot; a Statoil spokesman said.</p>
<p>On Saturday the field produced 38,932 cubic metres of oil, or 244,882 barrels.</p>
<p>In July, Heidrun had an average daily output of 222,402 barrels.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
